# GitHub Student Profile

This project will introduce you to Git and GitHub.

You will:

1. Clone this repository to your computer.
2. Add information about yourself.
3. Commit your changes.
4. Push your changes to GitHub.
5. Make another change.
6. Commit and push again.
7. Look at your commit history.

## Important Git Concepts

### Repository
A project that Git is tracking.

### Clone
Makes a copy of a repository on your computer.

### Commit
Creates a snapshot of your changes.

### Push
Sends your commits from your computer to GitHub.

### Pull
Gets changes from GitHub onto your computer.

## Your Assignment

### Part 1 — Create Your Profile

Edit `profile.txt` and add your information.

Save the file.

Open GitHub Desktop and look at the changes Git detected.

Commit your changes with the message:

`Added my profile`

Push your commit to GitHub.

### Part 3 — Look at Your History

Go to your repository on GitHub.

Find the section showing your commits.

You should see at least two commits.
